From: greyoak111 <151205158+greyoak111@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:52:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 46/49] Updates: beta channel, skipping a version, rollback
 with settings backups

- Beta: an opt-in option also offers pre-releases (the release list instead
  of the latest stable release).
- Skip: a skipped version is left alone by automatic mode; a manual check
  still shows it and downloading it clears the skip.
- Every install first backs up OBS's settings (scenes, profiles, plugin
  settings; the newest 8 are kept) under Application Support/LiveHime/
  backups, and keeps the replaced app. "Roll back" puts it back, skips the
  version left, and when the two use different OBS major versions restores
  the scenes, profiles and OBS ini files from before the update, since OBS
  migrates them forward only. An OBS major upgrade is announced before it
  installs.

e2e-update.mjs now covers the stable/beta choice, skipping, the settings
backup, and a rollback across OBS major versions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
